From efd02f0004242f6ad3a392c5259a9ea46be4d8ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Law <jeffreyalaw@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:59:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [PR rtl-optimization/128738] Ensure code is a CONST_INT
 before extracting its INTVAL

A simplify-rtx optimization added in the gcc-16 era can trip an RTL checking
failure and possibly a code generation correctness bug by accessing a register
node as a constant integer in a compiler without RTL checking.

The optimization in question is only valid of that object is a known constant
as we use the constant to create an adjusted mask, so require the object in
question to be a CONST_INT.  All the right things just happen after that.

Bootstrapped and regression tested on x86_64 and aarch64 overnight.

Pushing to the trunk and given the nature of the fix, I'm going to push to
gcc-16 now too.

	PR rtl-optimization/128738
gcc/
	* simplify-rtx.cc (simplify_context::simplify_binary_operation_1):
	For IOR of multiple single bit bitfields, ensure the second operand
	of OP1's AND is a CONST_INT.

gcc/testsuite
	* gcc.dg/torture/pr128738.c: New test.

(cherry picked from commit b6f87b7b2d286ef37c9179cb3b4c9490b8421cd7)
---
 gcc/simplify-rtx.cc                     | 3 ++-
 gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128738.c | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128738.c

diff --git a/gcc/simplify-rtx.cc b/gcc/simplify-rtx.cc
index e2c924f0205c..1454a19f12e0 100644
--- a/gcc/simplify-rtx.cc
+++ b/gcc/simplify-rtx.cc
@@ -3753,7 +3753,8 @@ simplify_context::simplify_binary_operation_1 (rtx_code code,
 	  && XEXP (op0, 1) == CONST1_RTX (mode)
 	  && XEXP (op1, 1) == CONST0_RTX (mode)
 	  /* Verify bit position. */
-	  && CONST_INT_P (XEXP (XEXP (op0, 0), 1)))
+	  && CONST_INT_P (XEXP (XEXP (op0, 0), 1))
+	  && CONST_INT_P (XEXP (XEXP (op1, 0), 1)))
 	{
 	  unsigned HOST_WIDE_INT bitpos1 = INTVAL (XEXP (XEXP (op0, 0), 1));
 	  unsigned HOST_WIDE_INT mask
diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128738.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128738.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..2090977e0737
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.dg/torture/pr128738.c
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+/* { dg-do compile } */
+int f(int x, int m) { return ((x >> 1) & 1) | ((x & m) != 0); }
+
